		(uuid "027dff2a-4c2b-4e3a-8dcb-149068e40c7d")
	)
  (text "Buzzer low-side switch: Q701 AO3400A (SOT-23, 30 V, 5.7 A, ~28 mOhm) - headroom\nfor louder / higher-current buzzers vs the old 2N7002.  Gate from BUZZER (PB8)\nwith R701 10k pull-down.  D701 1N4148W flyback across the buzzer, cathode to +5V.\nJ704: 1=+5V  2=buzzer- (BUZZ_N)."
    (at 45 62 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "ebee8868-d886-4ac4-a373-6073a76957f6")
  )
  (text "J705 LED strip - WS2812.  D702 (S2M, 2 A silicon rectifier, SMA) in series on\nstrip VDD: 5 V - ~0.7 V @ 0.5 A -> strip runs at ~4.3 V, so WS2812 VIH\n(~0.7*VDD ~= 3.0 V) is within reach of the 3V3 LED_DATA line (PA8 via R702 330R).\nA Schottky (~0.3 V) would give ~4.7 V and leave VIH marginal - silicon is required.\nReal current limit: the JST-SH connector (SM03B-SRSS-TB, 1 A / contact) caps strip\ndraw at ~1 A = roughly 16 WS2812 at full white (~60 mA each).  D702 must be rated\nabove that - S2M (2 A) clears it.  Feed a longer strip from its own 5 V, not J705.\n1=+5V (via D702)  2=GND  3=DATA (LED_STRIP via R702)."
    (at 115 160 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "67fbfd2f-47dd-4cd2-94c8-ec21627b120c")
  )
  (text "J703 aux I2C - shares I2C1 with U401 (DPS368).  Pull-ups are R401/R402 = 2.2k\non the baro sheet (sized for a cabled device here); do not add more.\nt_r with a cable ~= 186 ns -> OK for 400 kHz.\n1=+5V  2=GND  3=I2C1_SCL  4=I2C1_SDA."
    (at 120 118 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "4fc38469-a45e-487f-b9c0-203b9d0523fb")
  )
